content:
{
  "asset": "P-114 — AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-20500, on the raw-water transfer line",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing-housing vibration is 8.3 mm/s. Figure 3 is the applicable HF-300 bearing-housing vibration-velocity classification, expressed in mm/s RMS. On that basis, 8.3 exceeds the 7.1 mm/s RMS Zone C/D boundary and falls in Zone D (7.1–11.0 mm/s RMS, end of axis shown): damage likely — stop the pump. It is above Zone C's 4.5–7.1 restricted/plan-maintenance range.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing-housing temperature is 70 °C. The applicable limits are bearing-housing surface-temperature limits: normal up to 70 °C, alarm at 80 °C and trip at 90 °C. The reading is exactly at the upper normal value, 10 °C below alarm and 20 °C below trip; it is not a documented high-temperature reading and does not itself trigger bearing replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leakage is reported. The troubleshooting symptom leakage at shaft seal would require mechanical-seal replacement and an alignment check, but that symptom is not present; this report therefore does not establish a leakage-based need to replace the seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The available vibration classification is based on the drive-end reading only. The manual requires weekly velocity measurements on both bearing housings and classification of the highest reading; the non-drive-end reading is not available for comparison.",
      "citations": [
        "C06"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "The evidence does not support a likelihood ranking. The manual's documented high-vibration causes, in its listed order, are: (1) misalignment, (2) bearing wear, (3) impeller imbalance or damage, and (4) cavitation. The corresponding documented checks are shaft alignment, bearing and impeller inspection, and NPSH.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Immediately stop P-114 and keep it out of service while the applicable vibration classification remains Zone D. Do not restart it merely to obtain additional vibration measurements.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before mechanical disassembly, isolate and drain the pump in accordance with the manual's removal procedure. Where back pull-out removal is required, use the design feature that permits rotating-assembly removal without disturbing the casing or pipework, and provide lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Diagnose the high vibration: check shaft alignment, inspect the drive-end and non-drive-end bearings and the impeller, and check NPSH for possible cavitation. Record alignment results, bearing condition, impeller condition and NPSH findings before authorizing corrective parts beyond the conditional bearing-pair scope.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair: drive-end HF3-512 (6312-C3) and non-drive-end HF3-510 (6310-C3). Do not use the reported 70 °C housing temperature alone as the high-temperature trigger.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the casing is opened, install a new HF3-120 casing gasket. If mechanical-seal work is separately found necessary, follow procedure 5.2: remove the back pull-out assembly, impeller nut and impeller; withdraw the seal and sleeve; inspect the sleeve for scoring; and fit the new seal and a new casing gasket.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For disturbed fasteners, reassemble with lightly oiled threads to Table 5: M16 casing bolts 210 Nm; M24 impeller nut 160 Nm; M10 seal gland nuts 25 Nm for this serial number; and M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm. Apply each torque only where that fastener is disturbed.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser shaft alignment. Documented tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After corrective work, when operation is authorized for verification, measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading using Figure 3. Zone B is documented for long-term operation, Zone C is restricted/plan maintenance, and Zone D requires stopping. Also record the housing surface temperature and compare it with normal up to 70 °C, alarm 80 °C and trip 90 °C; escalate any unresolved restricted or stop-zone result rather than closing the work as normal.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3. Conditional: stage one only if inspection triggers the documented requirement to replace both bearings as a pair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3. Conditional: stage one with HF3-512 if either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket. Quantity one; replace whenever the casing is opened and when mechanical-seal replacement is performed.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop the pump immediately: the reported vibration falls in Figure 3's Zone D when assessed on the required RMS velocity basis, where damage is likely and the instruction is to stop the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before following the manual's back pull-out/mechanical-seal disassembly procedure. Site-specific isolation and lockout details remain an open question.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use lifting equipment for the back pull-out assembly; its documented mass is 68 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For any authorized operational verification, preserve the documented Seal Flush Plan 11 supply from pump discharge and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement as a pair, if required by inspection: standard allowance 6.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment after work that moves the motor or bearing housing: standard allowance 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If mechanical-seal replacement is separately authorized after inspection, its standard allowance is 4.0 hours with 2 technicians; it is not established as required by the current no-leakage report.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The manual parts list and Table 5 specify component seal HF3-450 and 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, whereas SB-2026-014 specifies HF3-450B and 30 Nm. The bulletin, issued 14 March 2026, applies only to HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above. P-114 is HF3-20500 and therefore below the cutoff: for this asset, retain HF3-450 and the manual's 25 Nm torque on lightly oiled threads if seal work is required; do not apply HF3-450B or 30 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The manual requires inspection of shaft sleeve HF3-455 for scoring, while SB-2026-014 gives a 0.1 mm scoring-depth replacement criterion within its instructions for pumps covered by that bulletin. Because HF3-20500 is below HF3-22000, do not treat the bulletin's 0.1 mm criterion or its HF3-450B pre-set/no-sleeve-measurement instruction as the documented requirement for this asset.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "The fault report does not explicitly state that the 8.3 mm/s vibration reading is RMS, although Figure 3's applicable limits are expressed in mm/s RMS. Confirm the instrument setting and measurement basis (C07).",
    "Only the drive-end vibration reading is supplied. Obtain the non-drive-end reading from existing safe monitoring records or post-repair verification; both housings are required for routine monitoring and the highest reading must be classified (C06).",
    "No alignment measurements, bearing wear/noise inspection results, impeller condition or NPSH/cavitation data are supplied. The actual cause, the need for bearing-pair replacement and any impeller corrective work therefore remain undetermined (C09, C10).",
    "The evidence calls for an NPSH check but provides neither the required NPSH value nor a test method or acceptance criterion. Obtain the applicable hydraulic/system data and acceptance criterion (C09).",
    "If the seal and sleeve are exposed and scoring is found, the manual provides no scoring-depth rejection limit for this below-HF3-22000 serial, and the bulletin's 0.1 mm criterion has not been applied to this asset. Obtain an engineering disposition before reusing or replacing the sleeve on that basis (C10, C13).",
    "Table 6 provides no standard time for diagnosis, inspection, NPSH investigation, impeller correction or operational verification, so a total job duration cannot be calculated until the corrective scope is known (C12).",
    "Site-specific isolation/lockout steps, permits and the detailed lifting plan are not included in the evidence; only isolation/draining and the requirement for lifting equipment for the 68 kg assembly are documented (C02, C10).",
    "The evidence does not define the site's P1/P2/P3 priority matrix. P1 is assigned here as a planning decision because Figure 3 explicitly requires an immediate stop for the applicable Zone D vibration condition (C07)."
  ]
}
